WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.877
This query uses two windows over the same employee rows.

00:00:03.877 --> 00:00:09.692
AVG salary with PARTITION BY department calculates the department average.

00:00:09.692 --> 00:00:14.972
ROW_NUMBER with partition and order assigns a sequence within each department.

00:00:14.972 --> 00:00:17.062
No GROUP BY is used.

00:00:17.062 --> 00:00:19.757
Every employee row remains in the output, with additional context beside it.

00:00:19.757 --> 00:00:27.227
When reading the example, do not read punctuation one character at a time.

00:00:27.227 --> 00:00:31.452
Start with the purpose of the query, then identify the input rows, the operation being applied,

00:00:31.452 --> 00:00:35.677
and the shape of the expected output.

00:00:35.677 --> 00:00:41.762
In a real setting such as a sales team calculating running revenue and top products by region,

00:00:41.762 --> 00:00:47.832
this habit makes code reviews much easier because you can explain what the query is supposed to guarantee

00:00:47.832 --> 00:00:49.867
before discussing syntax.

00:00:49.867 --> 00:00:55.984
After running it, inspect a few records manually and check that the result matches that explanation.
